<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Minimal Nav2 Humble behavior tree for the Nano: ComputePathToPose + FollowPath
  in a PipelineSequence, wrapped in a RecoveryNode with number_of_retries="1".

  Semantics (verified against Humble recovery_node.cpp): run Navigate; on
  FAILURE run the Recovery sequence ONCE (clear local + global costmaps, back
  up, spin), then retry Navigate; on a second failure abort.

  The ClearEntireCostmap service_name values MUST match the costmap node
  namespaces ("local_costmap/clear_entirely_local_costmap" /
  "global_costmap/clear_entirely_global_costmap"). BackUp/Spin actions are
  served by behavior_server's spin/backup plugins (nav2_params.yaml).

  User decision 2026-09-23: the recovery MOTIONS are zeroed (backup_dist 0,
  spin_dist 0) — a failed goal still clears the costmaps and retries ONCE,
  but the robot never physically backs up or spins (both behaviors complete
  immediately at zero distance/yaw; a web Recovery toggle that swapped BTs
  per goal was tried and reverted the same day). Restore motion by giving
  backup_dist/spin_dist real values here + restarting nano-nav (the tree
  loads at activation only).

  REACTIVE REPLANNING (2026-09-27, user decision): ComputePathToPose runs ONCE
  at goal start and the robot follows that path; a blocked path reroutes via
  the RecoveryNode retry (clear costmaps -> fresh plan). The previous
  RateController hz="1.0" (added 2026-09-24 when the costmaps had no live
  obstacle feed) replanned every second, and PipelineSequence HALTS FollowPath
  for each replan — on this CPU a full-resolution Smac plan + SmoothPath action
  costs 0.3-0.45 s, so the robot coast-paused ~380 ms EVERY second (measured
  2026-09-27: 27 pauses in 42 s = ~25% of drive time; the dominant residual
  stutter). The live ObstacleLayer (both costmaps, 2026-09-24) now marks
  new/moved objects within ~1 s and RPP's collision-ahead check stops the
  robot, so the stale-plan-into-obstacle failure the 1 Hz replan guarded
  against is covered reactively.
  TRADE-OFF (accepted): a path blocked by an object that APPEARS mid-drive
  reroutes only after the progress checker fails FollowPath
  (movement_time_allowance 15 s in nav2_params.yaml) — slower than proactive
  rerouting, but zero pauses on clear paths. To restore proactive replanning,
  wrap ComputePathToPose back in <RateController hz="1.0"> (the plugin is
  still in plugin_lib_names; the default through-poses tree bt_navigator
  validates at activation uses it).
-->
<root main_tree_to_execute="MainTree">
  <BehaviorTree ID="MainTree">
    <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="1" name="NavigateRecovery">
      <PipelineSequence name="Navigate">
        <ComputePathToPose goal="{goal}" path="{path}" planner_id="GridBased"/>
        <FollowPath path="{path}" controller_id="FollowPath"/>
      </PipelineSequence>
      <Sequence name="Recovery">
        <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearLocal" service_name="local_costmap/clear_entirely_local_costmap"/>
        <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearGlobal" service_name="global_costmap/clear_entirely_global_costmap"/>
        <BackUp backup_dist="0" backup_speed="0.1"/>
        <Spin spin_dist="0"/>
      </Sequence>
    </RecoveryNode>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
